@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security;verification] omnios-offline-candidate
The native candidate kit MUST bind every installed file and symlink, the exact
pinned stock raw image and native interpreter. Native installation MUST require
a separate unimported scratch pool, clone the original BE, preserve its loader
and GPT/ZFS disk, and attempt clean export. A refused export MUST preserve the
workspace for recovery. The running root MUST never be a target.
The exact regular sudoers kit bytes MUST be installed root:root mode0440 with
non-symlink target and ancestors, and the secondboot payload receipt MUST bind
that target mode independently of immutable Nix source permissions.
The kit manifest MUST bind final Nix-published regular-file modes0444/0555,
never temporary builder write permissions that disappear at publication.
Assembly MUST apply the reviewed site profile only to the scratch clone's SMF
repository, disabling all four stock cloud-init instances and stock SSH. The
clone's two fixed stock manifests MUST enter a seed repository before profile
application. SVCCFG_REPOSITORY and the repository command MUST bind the same
validated clone repository, so offline imports never await the live restarter.
The second boot MUST verify each instance remains disabled; Overalls MMDS bootstrap
owns the static network and the roster-bound supervisor owns native SSH.
The scratch clone MUST preserve its stock configuration and append pseudo_isa=1
in /etc/system plus console/os_console=ttya and 115200,8,n,1,- ttya mode in the
pinned loader's /boot/loader.conf.local. Exact final configuration digests and
modes MUST enter the payload receipt and secondboot verification. This serial
handoff MUST NOT add debugger, singleuser, verbose boot or root autologin defaults.
Offline assembly MUST bind every initial CA file exactly. After boot, only
/etc/ssl/cacert.pem MAY transition to the reviewed root-owned managed bundle
link; its target MUST be a regular root:root mode0644 file in the fixed trust
directory with exact vendor prefix and one to 32 bounded public PEM roots.
/etc/overalls/system-ca.pem and all other static payloads MUST retain their exact
digests and modes. This structural verification MUST NOT claim current-boot trust
authority; the daemon's boot-bound installation receipt establishes that boundary.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] omnios-candidate-acceptance
Installation and second-boot kernel/module/getter verification MUST remain
distinct from complete native service, isolation, recovery and catalog evidence.
Neither the kit nor its receipts MAY open nativeAdmission or emit a production
manifest. The unchanged unix digest and the nine installed module digests MUST
remain separate identities; the eventual raw image digest binds their placement.
